  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Implemented and scale-hardened the claimed ordinary-Python spectral package: validated Hermitian and general eigensystems, reduced SVD, radix-2/Bluestein FFT, direct/FFT convolution, canonical CSR storage, certified-SPD CG/BiCGSTAB solves, and a gap-certified dominant Hermitian sparse eigenpair. All dense, transform, and sparse paths normalize finite inputs, use scale-safe norms and relative validation, rescale with exponent-aware arithmetic, and return structured validation_failed results without non-finite JSON when a finite mathematical output is not representable in binary64. General nonsymmetric eigensystems independently validate pivoted basis inversion, reciprocal condition, inverse residual, reconstruction, eigenpair residuals, and Schur factors; defective and near-defective bases fail closed with no value. Automatic sparse solves use CG only after a sufficient strict Hermitian diagonal-dominance SPD certificate, while uncertified/indefinite Hermitian inputs route to BiCGSTAB; sparse power iteration requires separated Gershgorin intervals and rejects equal-magnitude or zero spectra before iteration. Added SpectralResult with versioned JSON explanations, accessible text, and bounded renderer-neutral PlotSpec/PlotAnimation views for eigensystems, SVD, FFT, convolution, conditioning, convergence, and aliasing; views use only returned/retained evidence, cap static samples at 1024 and frames at 32, and record decimation or magnitude normalization. Added package-local side-effect-free supports/plan dispatch using detached capabilities and independently recorded sparse certificates. CPython/Sage.js tests cover extreme scale, failure, metamorphic, JSON, cancellation, maximum_elapsed_time, planning, explanations, accessibility, trace bounds, and visualization; the oracle retains 342 NumPy/SciPy comparisons with maximum absolute difference 1.0658141036401503e-14. Refreshed strict checks, benchmark/payload evidence, capability classifications, and documentation.",
    "risks": [
      "Four-platform qualification remains an integration/release responsibility; focused receipts in this task are Linux x64.",
      "The full architecture aggregate remains an integration responsibility: the synchronized numerical foundation has a shared native-boundary inventory change outside this lane's claims.",
      "pnpm test:changed stops at merge:check because src/lib/sagejs/numerics/spectral/__init__.py has no shared package-graph owner. All eight modules pass focused Pyright and repository strict-Python checks but are intentionally not yet listed in the shared pyrightconfig because both registries are outside this lane's claims.",
      "This lane emits the exact maximum_elapsed_time stop and diagnostic. The integration lane must add that exact spelling to shared STATUS_CODES and the diagnostic registry before exercising a public elapsed-time result."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "In the integration lane, add a lazy numerical-spectral package-graph component (layer 5, at least a 220000-byte source budget) for prefix src/lib/sagejs/numerics/spectral/, module sagejs.numerics.spectral, depending on core-runtime, python-stdlib, and numerical-computing (which already owns the PlotSpec dependency).",
      "In the integration lane, add exactly src/lib/sagejs/numerics/spectral/__init__.py, _common.py, dense.py, planning.py, result.py, sparse.py, transforms.py, and visualization.py to pyrightconfig.json; register test/numerics/spectral/spectral-laboratory.cjs, spectral-visualization.cjs, and strict-python.cjs in the appropriate shared test/package ownership records; and connect the package-local capabilities, supports, and plan functions to the central lazy numerical facade.",
      "In the integration lane, add maximum_elapsed_time exactly to src/lib/sagejs/numerics/model.py STATUS_CODES and src/lib/sagejs/numerics/diagnostics.py with execution-phase warning semantics; do not alias it to maximum_evaluations.",
      "Regenerate and review the shared native-boundary inventory for the inherited numerical-optimization callback probe, then rerun pnpm architecture:check, pnpm test:changed, and the required four-platform qualification."
    ]
  }
